-- Five cities that already have five or more rows (three groups each) get an intro and are published
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Naperville and the Fox Valley towns of Batavia and Geneva play American mahjong at breweries, restaurants and cafes. Mariposa Mahjong and Blue Tiger Mahj Club run evening sessions where newcomers learn American Mahjong, with guided play and Mahjong 102 afternoons, and Mindful Mah Jongg asks players to bring a 2026 NMJL card. Events are ticketed through Eventbrite and the venues change, so check each listing. If you are new, start with an Introduction to Mahjong evening.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'naperville';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Rochester''s American mahjong centers on the Louis S. Wolk JCC, which runs a beginner class and a play-only Mah Jongg Club. Its class page says the instructors, Richard Collier-Morris and John Kinnicutt, cover the official National Mah Jongg League rules. The club meets in the Erdle Lounge, and class dates change, so check the JCC''s listing. The class is for people who have never played, so start there before you join the club.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'rochester';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Denton has a social club with beginner classes, a free church open play and a Little Elm group that plays at TinMan Social. Winds of Laughter asks players to bring a 2026 National Mahjongg card, the Texan Trippers hold free open play at First United Methodist Church for players who already know the game, and North Texas Mahjong runs an American Mahjong Foundations workshop. Check each listing for times and venues. If you are new, start with the Foundations workshop or a Winds of Laughter beginner class.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'denton';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'On the East End of Long Island, American mahjong turns up at restaurants, cafes and an arts center. Southampton Arts Center runs six-week workshops for beginners and intermediate players, Montauk Mahj hosts Friday afternoon games over Lake Montauk, and mahjong lunches and happy hours are held at restaurants from East Hampton to Montauk. Quogue Library has offered a beginner course too. Dates change with the season, so check each listing. If you are new, the Southampton Arts Center workshop is the place to start.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'southampton';
UPDATE "City" SET "published" = 1, "intro" = 'Ocean Springs and D''Iberville on the Mississippi Gulf Coast have a few small clubs that play on the 2026 NMJL card. The Tile Parlour hosts afternoons of American Mahjong at Crave Food Hall in downtown Ocean Springs, OS Mahj Club asks players to bring tile sets and the NMJL 2026 card, and Bam Time Mahj Parlor holds a Thursday Tile Party in D''Iberville. Events change often, so check each listing. If you are new, message a club first and ask which table suits beginners.', "updatedAt" = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE "slug" = 'ocean-springs';
